SUSPECTED BUG: middleware chain built in a loop, stored in a map, called dynamically. Business routes are
Recover(MapErrors(Translate)(Deadline(Auth(h)))), /health is the swallow-all handler. Correct set: *api.Error (404 no
route + Translate's sites), api.ErrUnavailable, ErrDuplicate behind (*api.Error).Unwrap, Recover's opaque "middleware:
panic serving %s: %v"; ErrUnauthorized, ctx errors and domain errors only translated. Actual: every Handler value is a
Candidate of every Handler call (7 candidates), so untranslated *ValidationError, NotFoundError, ErrBusy, audit errors ...
are reported, the chain becomes one cycle that hits unresolved(fixpoint-limit) (>1024 values), and the cut set is
arbitrary: 206 of the 209 entries come from the handleTransfer / handleBalance Candidates, while Translate's *api.Error
values, api.ErrUnavailable and middleware.ErrUnauthorized - the errors Serve really returns - are all missing.
(Chain returns h itself when mws is empty, so a flow-insensitive Candidate set for Chain's result must contain the
raw handlers; the suspected bug is the cut that drops the real origins, not that over-approximation alone.)
-- args --
-fanout=2 api/api.go:@serve
